##THREADS MARKETING AND AUDIENCE BUILDING
Once your ebook is uploaded to Gumroad, the next step is to attract potential customers through Threads. The goal is to build an audience by sharing useful content, starting conversations and gradually introducing your ebook as a solution.



Research Successful Creators - 
Before posting, study creators who are already building an audience in your niche.

How to do it:
Search for keywords related to your niche on Threads.
Follow around 10 established creators in your niche.
Explore their most engaging posts and conversations.
Study their hooks, writing styles, storytelling and post formats.
Identify the problems and topics that receive the most engagement.
Use these observations to develop your own original content ideas.



Create Value-Based Content - 
Don't make every post about selling your ebook. First, provide useful information that attracts your target audience and establishes trust.

Types of content you can publish:
Tips and Advice: Share practical tips related to your niche.
Step-by-Step Guides: Explain how to solve specific problems.
Personal Experiences: Share genuine experiences, lessons and mistakes.
Case Studies: Discuss real examples and results.
Lists: Create posts such as "5 mistakes beginners make when starting a business."
Questions: Ask questions that encourage people to share their experiences.
Free Resources: Share useful templates, checklists and frameworks.



Create Promotional Posts (Soft Selling) - 
Along with value-based content, occasionally introduce your ebook through promotional posts.

How to do it:
Identify a problem that your ebook helps solve.
Create a post explaining the problem and offering a useful insight.
Briefly mention that you've created a detailed guide covering the topic.
Add a clear call to action (CTA).
Direct interested readers to the product link in your bio.

Example:
"Struggling to find internships as a college student?
Start by improving your resume, building your LinkedIn profile and reaching out to relevant companies.
I have put together a complete step-by-step guide covering the entire process. You can find it through the link in my bio."



Maintain a Consistent Posting Schedule - 
Consistency helps you stay visible and gives you more opportunities to reach potential customers.

Suggested daily posting strategy: 
8–10 value-based posts.
2 promotional or soft-selling posts.
You can adjust this frequency based on your available time and audience response. Focus on quality rather than posting just to meet a number.



Engage With Your Audience - 
Threads is a conversation-based platform, so don't limit your activity to publishing posts.

How to do it:
Reply to comments on your own posts.
Participate in discussions related to your niche.
Leave meaningful replies on posts from established creators.
Answer questions from potential customers.
Follow relevant accounts and build genuine connections.
Use audience questions to discover new content and ebook ideas.



Use Strong Hooks and Calls to Action - 
The opening line of your post should encourage people to stop scrolling and read further.

Examples of hooks:
"Most beginners make this mistake when..."
"Here's something I wish I knew earlier..."
"If you're struggling with ___, read this."
"5 things you should know before starting..."
"Nobody talks about this when it comes to..."

End relevant posts with a CTA that encourages replies, profile visits or product discovery.



Things to Keep in Mind - 
Focus on providing value before promoting your ebook.
Avoid making every post a sales pitch.
Experiment with different hooks and post formats.
Don't copy other creators' posts; develop your own original versions.
Maintain a consistent posting schedule.
Build genuine relationships with your audience.
Give your strategy time to work rather than expecting immediate sales.



Useful tools:
Threads – Content publishing and audience engagement.
ChatGPT – Post ideas, hooks, captions and content drafts.
Google Sheets / Notion – Content planning and scheduling.
